  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pb</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi></mover><mi>PbO</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gas is constituent of air and it produces ammonia gas (basic nature) after reacting with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gas.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>NaN</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo></math>give nitrogen gas on heating but lead nitrate doesn&#39;t give nitrogen gas so it will be answer.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O<